# covers: 0b 1.5, 1a 2.5
# 0b-login-replaces-a: runs with 0b-login-replaces-b under run-sim-multi.sh; both log in as the
# SAME account (nf.LoginGroup) and so the same character. A is first in; when B's session takes
# over the entity, A's socket is closed with 4409 (api-guidelines "Close codes") and A must NOT
# reconnect (that would replace B in turn).
#
# Timeouts (R1): B waits 15 s (the 3x login chain) before it enters, then needs its own 15 s
# chain; A waits 60 s for the close. The 4 s pause is > 3x the 0.5 s first reconnect backoff plus
# a ticket round trip.
nf.LoginGroup
nf.WaitFor connected 15
nf.EnterWorld
nf.WaitFor in_world 15
nf.WaitFor close_code == 4409 60
nf.Sleep 4
nf.Expect ws_closed               # no automatic reconnect
nf.Expect own_spawns == 1         # a reconnect would have produced a second spawn stream
nf.Within 120
